WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.910
From the opening frames, it's clear that writer/director
Rian Johnson planned to take The Last Jedi

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.370
into a galaxy far, far away from every Star
Wars film preceding it.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.950
That's true for both the story and the characters
who made that story happen.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.019
While some of them didn't get a lot of time
in front of the audience, they definitely

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:19.560
contributed to the saga—often more than
you might realize.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.680
Here are all the characters in Star Wars:
The Last Jedi who mean more than you think.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.770
General Hux

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.320
In The Force Awakens, the whole First Order
thing kind of feels like an excuse to keep

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.210
having stormtroopers, even though they shouldn't
have been around anymore.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.170
Since, you know, they were basically Ewok
tom-toms at the end of Episode 6.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.940
Well, as with anything Star Wars, there's
a lengthy backstory now as to how the First

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.420
Order came to be, and it all started with
General Hux.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.879
In both The Force Awakens and The Last Jedi,
Hux serves as the head military honcho who

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:49.969
essentially took the place of Moff Tarkin.

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:54.440
But he's actually a big reason why the First
Order exists in the first place.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.850
The novel Phasma describes how Hux was a child
when the Empire was defeated.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.569
He traveled into exile with his father and
started cultivating what became the First

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:05.680
Order using the ideology of the defunct Empire.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.590
With Captain Phasma, he concocted a plan to
assassinate his father.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.100
About ten years after that, Hux was a general
in charge of Starkiller Base, and the rest

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.619
is cinematic history.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:20.340
But judging by the meager screentime he gets,
fans probably wouldn't guess that Hux is directly

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.040
responsible for all of this.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.740
And while we're on the topic of the First
Order…

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.350
Captain Phasma

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.970
The first question savvy fans might have after
watching The Last Jedi is, why the heck wasn't

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.149
Captain Phasma punished after basically letting
the Resistance waltz onto Starkiller Base

00:01:36.149 --> 00:01:38.659
and lower the defensive shields in The Force
Awakens?

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:43.340
Well, first off, in the comic Captain Phasma,
we learn that Phasma simply went into the

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.999
computer system and framed a lowly lieutenant
for that little security breach.

00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:49.009
Easy peasy.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:53.020
Secondly, Phasma actually holds a lot more
sway in the First Order than the films let

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.020
on.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.159
Aside from Supreme Leader-slash-hobgoblin
Snoke, the First Order is controlled by what

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:04.719
StarWars.com calls a "triumvirate" of commanders–Kylo
Ren, General Hux, and Captain Phasma.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:08.869
Phasma's specific job is to oversee all the
stormtroopers in the First Order.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:13.280
She also occasionally steps in and personally
trains some of the troopers, notably the FN

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.620
Corps –which you might recognize as Finn's
unit.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.100
Phasma personally trained the turncoat who
helps destroy almost everything the First

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.230
Order throws at the Resistance, so to say
that she plays a crucial role in the story

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.290
is putting it mildly.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.150
Vice Admiral Holdo

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:32.290
Laura Dern's character, Vice Admiral Holdo,
began the movie as something as a thorn in

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.770
Dameron's side, but it's safe to say that
by the end of it she totally redeemed herself.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:43.820
"You go and do something like this, AND TOTALLY
REDEEM YOURSELF!"

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:51.280
The Last Jedi is the first time we've seen
this character onscreen, but Holdo actually

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.129
has a long history with Leia.

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:55.400
As in, they're basically childhood friends.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:00.700
According to the young adult novel Leia, Princess
of Alderaan, Holdo first met Leia on Coruscant

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.269
the same year the events of The Empire Strikes
Back take place.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:07.800
Holdo soon learned about Leia's involvement
in the Rebellion, and even helped her on a

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.019
few missions during those early years.

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:14.040
When Leia got around to setting up the Resistance
in the years before The Force Awakens, her

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.311
old friend Holdo was one of Leia's first choices
to help lead the rebels against the First

00:03:18.311 --> 00:03:19.311
Order.

00:03:19.311 --> 00:03:22.900
So even though she's never been on a movie
screen before The Last Jedi, Holdo has been

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.050
part of the saga since the beginning.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.219
Maz Kanata

00:03:27.219 --> 00:03:31.959
First introduced in The Force Awakens, goggle-eyed
Maz Kanata seems to know just about everyone

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:33.560
and everything in the galaxy.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:38.180
The pirate queen obviously lives an adventurous
life, as evidenced by her brief, explosive

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.810
cameo in The Last Jedi.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.739
When we first meet her, Han Solo mentions
that she's had her castle for "a thousand

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:44.739
years."

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:48.290
So she's been around, but how much exactly
has Kanata seen?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.670
Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary
suggests that Kanata was well known by the

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.590
Empire during the years of the original trilogy.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:59.450
Even more intriguing, though, is the idea
that Kanata has seen just about the entire

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.730
history of the Star Wars universe–and been
a pretty prominent figure during a lot of

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.730
it.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.240
In fact, the first time fans ever laid eyes
on her wasn't in The Force Awakens.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.180
In The Phantom Menace, you can glimpse a statue
of what's believed to be Kanata in Anakin's

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.680
bedroom on Tatooine.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.190
According to the Star Wars Twitter account,
it's an alien pirate, and Anakin got the statue

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.350
from a trader passing through Mos Espa.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:25.270
Sure, it's a little far-fetched, but Maz is
an alien pirate who's something of a legend.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.410
If that is Maz, then even within the Star
Wars universe she's cool enough to get her

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.410
own action figures.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.360
And baby Darth Vader had one.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.030
He probably played with it all the time.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.030
DJ

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:41.380
Benicio del Toro's character of DJ the codebreaker
was teased months before the film came out,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.660
and his extended cameo in The Last Jedi didn't
disappoint.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:48.920
If anything, it left fans wanting more, and
Disney is stepping up to the challenge.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.780
If you thought there was more to DJ's story
than The Last Jedi revealed, you're completely

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:53.780
right.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:58.910
January 2018 will see the release of an exclusive
comic book detailing his backstory.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.790
Since he seems to know so much about how the
First Order and Resistance are funded, we're

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:06.790
guessing he's been involved with the ongoing
war for a long while.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.000
Thanks for watching!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.060
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.560
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

